  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a severe upward bias when historical volatility is high and sentiment remains neutral (0.00), failing to capture sudden price spikes.",
    "Forecasts systematically underestimate extreme upside events, often predicting smooth linear growth instead of the observed jagged, volatile paths seen in true outcomes.",
    "When recent history shows a range-bound pattern (e.g., 76-81 EUR) with zero sentiment, the model fails to anticipate volatility expansion and subsequent price surges beyond the historical high.",
    "The forecast horizon is overly smooth; corrections should introduce higher variance and potential for sharp upward jumps in the first 5-10 days of the forecast window.",
    "Neutral sentiment combined with a flat or slowly rising forecast trajectory indicates a high probability of mean reversion failure, where prices will overshoot the model's projected path."
  ]
}
